# ALLOWLIST, deliberately. ~/.claude holds session transcripts (projects/, 313MB), every
# prompt ever typed (history.jsonl), and real credentials (sessions/*.key, daemon/control.key).
# A denylist here is one forgotten pattern away from committing a secret or a prod query
# result, so: ignore everything, then re-admit only hand-picked config.
#
# Adding something new? Add an explicit `!` line for it. Never relax the leading `*`.

*

# --- config worth versioning -------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md
!settings.json
!statusline-command.sh
!keybindings.json

!hooks/
!hooks/**
!skills/
!skills/**
!commands/
!commands/**
!agents/
!agents/**
!local/
!local/**
!rules/
!rules/**
!bin/
!bin/claude-gc

# --- but never these, even inside the directories above ----------------------------
# settings.local.json can carry machine-local secrets (an API key was found in a repo's
# copy of this file on 2026-08-25).
settings.local.json
**/settings.local.json
*.key
*.pem
*credentials*
*token*
*secret*
# Any .env is ignored by DEFAULT — a new one is assumed to carry secrets until proven
# otherwise. Re-admit individually, as below, only after checking the values.
*.env
.env.*
# Re-admit a repo's ci-watch config once checked (CI_WATCH_WORKFLOW + CI_WATCH_LABEL only). Keep the
# comment on its own line: a trailing comment on a pattern line becomes part of the pattern.
#!local/<repo>-ci.env
# The per-user overlay (checked: author, branch patterns, test runner; no secrets) and its example.
!local/kit.env
!kit.env.example

# The shared tokenizer every Bash guard sources; it matches `*token*` above.
!hooks/lib/cmd-tokens

# Build/compile noise and vendored blobs that happen to sit under a tracked directory.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
local/artifacts/

# Machine output, not config: harness-synced skills and per-session digests.
skills/synced/
local/session-digests/

# Backups of tracked files: git is the history now, so these stop being created.
*.bak
*.bak-*
.*.bak-*

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
